# Release-archive exclusions (`git archive`, and therefore GitHub's "Source code"
# tarballs, honour `export-ignore`).
#
# `packaging/` is excluded because `packaging/daer.plan.toml` pins the SHA-256 of the
# release tarball it is used to build. If the plan were inside that tarball, the digest
# would have to describe a file containing itself: changing the digest changes the
# archive, which changes the digest. There is no fixed point, so the package could never
# verify its own source. Excluding the directory makes the digest computable and stable —
# and it is the honest boundary anyway, since a build recipe is not an input to the build
# it describes. `docs/`, `crates/` and `ebpf/` stay in: the package compiles and reads them.
packaging/ export-ignore
